{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1482618-looking-for-players-cairo-by-night-2022-text-based","id":1482618,"title":"Looking for Players: Cairo by Night 2022 (text based)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-01T11:06:10-07:00","id":1482618,"title":"Looking for Players: Cairo by Night 2022 (text based)","content":"Hi all. I am recruiting players for my text based campaign CAIRO BY NIGHT 2022: THE TRIUMPHANT CITY. This is the pitch. <br /> INTRODUCTION <br /> In the year 2000 a &quot;fake Gehena&quot; event, known as the Week of Nightmares, destroyed around a fifth of the Kindred global population, and nearly a third of the Middle Eastern one. The city of Cairo was one of the most affected in the world, with almost half its undead inhabitants wiped out. <br /> Most survivors refuse to talk about what happened, but it's obvious that it left them scarred emotionally. For around one year most Kindred thought the End of Times had arrived. For up to five years more, half of them were still getting ready for the Apocalypse. At the end, nothing happened and the millenaristic hype fizzled out in the midst of a century full of developments in the world of the kine: 9/11 and the War in Terror, the rise of the Internet, 2008's financial crisis, the Arab Spring and the Global COVID Pandemic...<br /> Now it is the year 2022 and it has become clear to everyone but the most crackpot that this is not the end of the world, but the beginning of a new era, full of danger but also of opportunity. Cairo 's inmortal population has risen again and the nights at the city that used to be called the Triumphant are vibrant with new, energetic blood, too busy making a place for themselves to be worried about the relics from the past.<br /> Cairo is one of the most cosmopolitan cities for the Kindred. Located on the crossroads between \u00c1frica and the Middle East, with a strong European influence on its recent past, it hosts Ashirra, Camarilla and even a few Laibon Kindred. It is well known that its liberal Prince, the most powerful and oldest Caitiff in the world, allows the Anarchs, the Thin Bloods and even the Sabbat in his domain, as long as they follow his rules and keep the peace, and that the Banu Haqim, the Walid Set and an old sect known as the Tal'mahe'ra hold territory and seats at the Prince's Council. Word says that only the Giovanni and their allies are banned from the city, and no one knows why. <br /> With one leg on its glorious and mysterious past and the other on its promising future as a regional power in a nascent multipolar world, Egypt is also on the crossroads between the Old and the New. Where will it go? Will it sink in the sand or shoot for the stars? It is still early to know, but maybe a handful of Neonates will have a say on this.<br /> GAMEPLAY<br /> The campaign will follow a sandbox style, with a starting adventure to introduce the setting and create a narrative link among the PC's, and a week by week scene selection and strategic planning homebrewed system afterwards. Events will be set in motion by the PC's actions and by a secret engine that will keep the environment dynamic.<br /> Gameplay itself will be done 100% via text message in a dedicated Discord server, with different channels and threads to keep things happening in a semi simultaneous way, that aims to combine depth, player involvement and a dynamic pace. Synchronization will not be required, but the option to do it at least ocasionally will be valued. <br /> SYSTEM<br /> The base will be V20, with a few adaptations for simplicity and to accommodate it to a text based system. Combat will be greatly simplified and abstracted most of the time and many social and most perception based rolls will be made by the GM and its results included seamlessly in the text descriptions. <br /> PC'S OPTIONS<br /> Many options from many sourcebooks will be available, always depending on ST's final approval. As a rule of thumb assume most Clan and Bloodlines, Camarilla, Ashirra and Laibon Legacies and even Thin Bloods will be available.<br /> LORE AND METAPLOT<br /> Most Metaplot from the Revised Era has been ignored, so most Clans, Sects and Bloodlines are in a similar position to the one they had in the early 1990's. On the other hand, a homebrewed Metaplot event (albeit with an official metaplot name) has been introduced and some others may have happened or be happening in the background.<br /> Some significant changes have been made to the official Lore. The most obvious are that Vicissitude is no longer a Discipline at all and that the Followers of Set have been seriously remade into a more nuanced Clan. A lot of the WoD backstory and elements have been trimmed and altered to create mystery and suspense even among veteran players and ST's. <br /> 2001 CAIRO BY NIGHT<br /> The 2001 official module Cairo by Night has been in the base for the design of this campaign. It's geography section, basic political structure and some NPC's have been straight taken from this book. On the other hand many more elements, from Theme and Mood, up to many NPC's backstories, stats and motivations have been completely changed or even removed. And of course, many elements, including more than a hundred NPC's and a dozen Coteries have been added.<br /> SECURITY AGREEMENT<br /> Before the campaign starts all players will have to accept on a consensustwd Security Agreement to make sure everyone is being safe and having fun. The campaign has been designed with mature but not extreme content in mind, and that is the way I would like to keep it. <br /> ABOUT MYSELF<br /> I am a veteran VtM ST with a few campaigns in the 1990's under my belt. I have recently returned to the game and have been STimg a very enjoyable text based campaign for a few months. <br /> HOW TO PLAY<br /> If you are interested in playing, please DM me and I will send my Discord ID so we can start the player selection and character creation process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27429,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","user":"Microcuchon","date":". 06-01-2022, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T03:38:28-07:00","id":1482917,"title":"","content":"A couple excerpts from the character creation process: <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>ASHIRRA: </b>The character is a follower of the basic tenets of the dominant sect in the Muslim countries from Mauretania to Indonesia. Their basic tenets are very similar to the Camarilla ones, with the main differences being Ahirras' religious outlook and decentralized organizational style.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bay't: Majnoon (Malkavian), Mujrim (Ravnos), Mushakis (Brujah), Mutasharid (Nosferatu), al-Khayal (Lasombra), Ray'een al-Fen (Toreador), Wah-sheen (Gangrel), others (ask, at ST's discrection).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>LAIBON: </b>The character was Embraced by a member of the African Legacies. Even though they have their own traditions, the ones who have abandoned their traditional territories tend to follow the Camarilla tenets or have converted to Islam and are nominally members of the Ashirra. On the other hand, their lineages have been apart from the Camarilla and Ashirra ones that they have their own set of disciplines and weaknesses.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Legacies: Akunanse, Children of Damballah, Guruhi, Ishtarri, Kinyonyi, Naglopers (2), Osebo, Shango, Xu Dundu, Ramanga, others (ask, at ST's discrection).</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>APPENDIX 6: STARTING COTERIES </b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Elysium Attendants</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Requisites: Status 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The main social coterie for Camarilla Elders, ambitious Neonates and some artistically inclined Ashirra.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Nazrudin's Listeners</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Requistes: Status 1 or Ashirra Prestige 1 or Malkavian (any) Prestige 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The mansion of the Cairo Ulema (Muslim Wise Man) serves as a social meeting point for the Ahirra and a few Camarilla characters.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Aziz's Audience</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Requisites: Contacts 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Mongolian Baiti, cursive\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The best storyteller in Cairo's itinerant perfomances attract a mixed crowd from all walks of life and unlife.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}